            <ArticleTitle>Sedation and analgesia for the mechanically ventilated patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-41, ix</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ccm.2008.09.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mechanically ventilated patients in the intensive care unit routinely require sedative and analgesic medications to manage pain and anxiety. These medications may have unpredictable effects with long-term use. Strategies that may help to improve patient outcomes include thoughtful selection of medications, use of objective sedation and pain scales, and implementation of protocolized sedation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
